# Verify Before Handoff

Do NOT ask the operator to open a URL, refresh a page, or confirm a visual fix
until the agent has:
1. Confirmed the server/process is running on the stated host:port.
2. Loaded the URL via the Cursor browser tool (or equivalent). This check is
   mandatory. If no such tool is available, say so explicitly and state what was
   verified instead; do not silently skip it.
3. Fixed connection-refused, blank page, 404, and obvious runtime errors found
   in that check.

Use runtime-injected test credentials for sign-in flows when the repo documents
them (never plaintext secrets). Report PASS/FAIL with concrete evidence. Never
outsource first-pass QA to the operator for issues the agent can reproduce
locally.
